 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? That's completely normal, especially if you' usually cooking for others. Do you want start with something you can make at home, or would you feel more at ease ordering in? A small book is perfect. It gives you something to hold and feels like a project, which is comforting. Nice choice. order feels weird, order half and share the ramen, that way you' not eating alone and they take the plastic wok. Good call. An oily pasta dish will hold onto the sauce better than a noodle soup, and it' easier to share.",
